clk: qcom: gcc-sm6225: GPLL10/11 are Lucid PLLs in FSM legacy mode

The camera TFE clocks run from GPLL10, which this driver programs as an
SM6115-style DEFAULT_EVO PLL. On Khaje it is a Lucid PLL like GPLL8 (the
stock kernel leaves CAL_L_VAL 0x44, CONFIG_CTL 0x20485699 and MODE bit 24,
FSM legacy mode, in it; downstream gcc-khaje agrees), so it never locks and
the TFE RCG fails to switch to it: "rcg didn't update its configuration",
camss "clock enable failed: -16", no frames from any camera. Same for
GPLL11.

Lucid had been tried here before and timed out: mainline's
clk_trion_pll_configure() ignores SUPPORTS_FSM_LEGACY_MODE, which the
downstream version honours. Set the bit there too.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c	2026-10-21 19:38:54.297639414 +0300
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c	2026-10-21 19:39:12.684052981 +0300
@@ -1749,6 +1749,10 @@
 	regmap_update_bits(regmap, PLL_MODE(pll), PLL_UPDATE_BYPASS,
 			   PLL_UPDATE_BYPASS);
 
+	if (pll->flags & SUPPORTS_FSM_LEGACY_MODE)
+		regmap_update_bits(regmap, PLL_MODE(pll), PLL_FSM_LEGACY_MODE,
+				   PLL_FSM_LEGACY_MODE);
+
 	/* Disable PLL output */
 	regmap_update_bits(regmap, PLL_MODE(pll),  PLL_OUTCTRL, 0);
 
